From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:26:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Present on a queue of its own

Metal 4 queues wait for a drawable on the GPU, until the display gives it
up, which may be the next refresh. Waiting on the main queue held up all
work behind the present, the next frame included, and bound the frame
rate to steps of the refresh interval with the GPU half idle: Medieval
Dynasty ran at 18 fps in game with 61 % GPU load.

Presents go to a second queue now, which waits for the main queue through
an event, so rendering continues while the drawable comes free. The image
the present blits from is safe: the application reuses it only after
acquiring a drawable, which the display releases once a later frame is
on screen. Medieval Dynasty runs at 27 fps, Green Hell's menu at 29
instead of 21. MESA_KK_PRESENT_QUEUE=0 presents on the main queue.

